let t = I(3)
---- exit code 1
error[Z0103]: no function is called `I`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | let t = I(3)
  |         ^ not a function of Zeff
  |
  = help: `zeff help` lists the functions of this release

====
let t = N(3)
---- exit code 1
error[Z0103]: no function is called `N`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | let t = N(3)
  |         ^ not a function of Zeff
  |
  = help: did you mean `n`?

====
let pi = 3
let y = p + 1
---- exit code 1
error[Z0101]: nothing is called `p` here
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:9
  |
2 | let y = p + 1
  |         ^ not a binding
  |
  = help: a bare name is a binding made with `let`; text is written in quotes, and a variable is named inside a frame's method, as in `wages.mean(wage)`

====
let d = frame(x = [1, 2], yy = [3, 4])
d.mean(y)
---- exit code 1
error[Z0101]: no variable `y` in `d`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:8
  |
2 | d.mean(y)
  |        ^ not a variable of d
  |
  = help: the variables of `d` are: x, yy

====
let d = frame(x = [1, 2], yy = [3, 4])
d.mean(X)
---- exit code 1
error[Z0102]: no variable `X` in `d`; names are case-sensitive
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:8
  |
2 | d.mean(X)
  |        ^ differs only in case from `x`
  |
  = help: write `x`

